# Tier D SC2025 per-track VIEW — derived 2026-08-07, NOT re-measured.
#
# PURPOSE: the set gate T4 is scored on (plan §8.3: "EXCEED Kissat-public PAR-2 on
# Tier D (SC25 set)"). Tier D itself is SC2024 + SC2025 (793 instances); this is the
# SC2025 main track alone, 400 instances.
#
# IT IS A SCORING VIEW, NEVER A SEPARATE RUN — the same rule the Tier C rule-neutral
# subset follows. Run Tier D once with every arm, then score it twice:
#
#     tools/bench/subset_score.py benchmarks/runs/<stamp>-D-<name> --subset D-sc25
#
# Running these 400 on their own would produce numbers not comparable to the full-tier
# window they came from, which is the whole reason the subset instrument exists.
#
# DERIVATION, mechanical and reproducible from the repo: benchmarks/tiers/D.sources
# carries D.list's per-track blocks, and its own header says they "are what a per-track
# (e.g. SC25-only, gate T4) score is reconstructed from". This list is
#     {main_2025 only: 393} union {shared, in BOTH main tracks: 7}  =  400,
# each line copied VERBATIM from D.list (path, expected verdict, reference time) so the
# two files cannot drift in format. All 400 were confirmed present in D.list at
# derivation time.
#
# The SC2024 complement is D.list minus this file (393); no separate list is kept for
# it, because no gate is scored on it.
#
# COMPOSITION CAVEAT (plan §11 O9): Tier D was frozen 2026-08-03 as SC2024+SC2025 and
# O9 asks for its composition to be revisited once SC2026 results land. That decision
# is owed before the T4 evaluation; it does not move this view, which is defined by
# what T4 names.
#
